
do not overcomplicate things
do not remove content unless specified
if code is being repeated, refactor into components and keep it in the same file unless otherwise specified

do not use flexbox to position things on typeset page, min-height: 100vh with flexbox causing the extra blank page issue. use padding-top instead when centering things on the page vertically

a03 fetch and html upload should go through the exact same cleaning, fetch/uploaded > you have a file > clean and treat that file the same > etc etc

pdf book pages rules:
- page 1 : h1 title and .author author, wrapped in a div, and centered on the page, horizontally and vertically
- page 2 : blank
- page 3: IF there is a second title and author, in the font size of the book, no bolding wrapped in a div, and centered on the page, horizontally and vertically, IF NOT, repeat h1 title and .author in the book text size
- page 4: blank
- page 5: summary if keeping + one blank page, otherwise STORY STARTS


## Code Editing Guidelines

### Preservation Rules
- NEVER remove existing UI sections, features, or functionality unless explicitly requested
- When making changes to a file, preserve all existing content that is not directly related to the requested change
- If a change requires modifying code near other sections, ensure those sections remain intact

### UI-Specific Rules
- UI sections are often organized in groups (headers, page numbers, formatting, etc.)
- When editing one UI section, verify adjacent sections are preserved in the replacement
- Check that closing tags, divs, and component wrappers remain balanced
- If a section seems to be missing after an edit, immediately add it back

### Verification Steps
- After any file edit, check that no unintended sections were removed
- If multiple similar sections exist (like checkboxes, radio buttons), ensure all are preserved unless specifically targeted
- Read the diff carefully before submitting changes